''We told them what we needed: a light weapon, more firepower, more rugged, easier to clean, less parts. Year later - no new guns, just new manuals. Told us to wrap our T24s with tape...''

Iwashitas were notorious for their complexity and tendency to lose parts during combat. Official manuals recommend using insulation tape to keep pins and screws from falling out.
^green;Field Fix: Higher durability than stock Iwashita T24 Rifle.^reset;
