''And we'll all feel gay, When Johnny comes marching home.''
Star Dust M4 with Special Operations Peculiar Modification II. Uses STANAG-NATO 5.56x45mm magazines.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''Arrows can be just as deadly as bullets.''
An advanced crossbow that follows similar patterns to a bolt-action rifle. Uses weighted bolts that can be stacked inside the crossbow's integrated magazine. Once the user fires a bolt, the user only needs to pull the handle back, allowing the next bolt to be loaded, letting the user fire a series of them in quick succession. ^yellow;Uses Weighted Bolts and deals THRUST damage.^reset;
^#c93d3d;Cannot MISS, but durability heavily impacts accuracy.^reset; 
^orange;Wall Defender: 0.5s PARRY WINDOW | 50HP STABILITY^reset;

''Fear is all we have left. Without it, we'll be nothing.''

The tengus would primarily use spears for hunting rather than weapons since they preferred their swords when it came to fighting. It was only when they began conscripting fairies in masses did they start using spears as a standard weapon.

^#FFEEC6;Impalement [SHIFT]: Charge forward with your spear and impale anything that gets in your way. | 15s Cooldown^white;

''Nothing is more permanent than a temporary solution.''

With the Indian situation dying down, and certain economic problems catching up with Japan, the IJA decided that a new 6.5x40mm rifle would be too costly to introduce right now, and that the current T30 rifle does the job just fine. The introduction of ''Year 34 Update Package'' hints that the problems with the upcoming ''Aichi 6.5x40mm Rifle'' were more political than monetary.
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''OTRINCO differs from other mega-corporations in that the weapons it sells actually comes from various manufacturing factories within the R.S.O. This means that there may be significant differences in quality between different weapons.''
OTRINCO QCQ171, chambered in 9x19mm.  It has a sort of Kurtz Maschinenpistole 5-like styling. though the internal mechanism is not the same. Holds 35rnds.
^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a questionable one-handed stance.^reset;

''Once a jolly swagman camped by the billabong.''
Submachine carbine chambered in 12.7x33mm (also known as .50AE). This firearm features two optional triggers—one forward and one backward-which are designed for use during single-handed and two-handed.
Uses 15rnd 12.7x33mm Magazines
^orange;Trooper: 1.0s PARRY WINDOW | 200HP STABILITY^reset;
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a versatile one-handed grip.^reset;

''One has to make do without gunpowder.''
Lightweight crossbow that fire flechettes rather than normal bolts. While the Kappas and Yamawaro did not possess the industrial base necessary to produce proper firearms for all their allies, they did have the tools necessary to improve what their allies did have to make the technological gap less wide. ^yellow;Uses Flechette Magazines and deals THRUST damage.^reset;
^#c93d3d;Cannot MISS, but durability heavily impacts accuracy.^reset;
^yellow;Has a high rate of fire but fires slow projectiles.^reset;

''Pick your fights wisely.''

A katana used by the youkai clans. Uses lightweight material to allow ease of one handed use at the cost of being slightly less durable than a traditional katana. Designed to be used in tangent with a shield.

^#FFEEC6;Retreating Slash [SHIFT]: Perform an extremely fast slash attack and leap back out of harm's way. | 5s Cooldown^reset;

''Strength is what determines who rule this land. That is how it's always been since the very beginning. The humans may think we are savages, but they are no different. Their guns and war machines is just another way for them to enforce their will. Nothing will change if they win.''

^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.5s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY.^white;
^#FFEEC6;Pummel [SHIFT]: Perform a powerful thrust forward which deals high BLUNT damage and stuns for 3 seconds. | 8s Cooldown^reset;

''Tenno Skoom!''

^orange;Cold-Blooded: 600HP STABILITY | 70% DEF.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user. Cannot perfect-block.^white;

''The enemy's greatest advantage is distance. Get close, and they'll be easy picking.''
Magilock pistol with two barrels instead of one. Sacrifices accuracy and reliability in favor of firing two shots. Rather than hit the target, these pistols were designed to fire as much magic as possible down range to make the enemies remain in cover until the user can force them into melee combat.
^yellow;Magishot ammunition determines damage and magazine capacity.^reset;
^#c93d3d;Cannot MISS, but durability heavily impacts accuracy.^reset;

''The question is not whether the shield will break, but whether the one holding it will.''

A heavy duty shield that is capable of taking enourmous punishment. Does not offer as much protection as other shields, but can remain standing even against gunfire if the user is strong enough to hold on to it.

^#CCD8B6;500HP STABILITY | 0.5s Lower-Raise Delay | 50% DEF.^white;

''They charged valiantly at us, thinking they had a chance. Reality however, isn't a fairytale. The moment they stepped into the open fields, we gunned them all down like the vermin they are.''

Traditional blade used by the tengu clans and youkai forces. Still see some use despite the dominating presence of firearms.

^#FFEEC6;Reckless Charge [SHIFT]: Lunge forward and perform a quick slash which deals high SLASH damage. | 5s Cooldown^reset;

''This is not the war, it's a special military operation.''
Used by the Unitan Special Forces and PMC Group. Based on the Avtomát Spetsiálny Val but without the integral suppressor. Only supports standard AS-VAL 9x39mm Magazines.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;
^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a questionable one-handed stance.^reset;

''War brings innovation. It also tends to bring a lot of questionable things with it as well. This is definetely one of them.''
Without industry, the Rose Empire had to make do with modifying what they had if they wanted to improve their equipment. With automatic firearms becoming the clear path forward in infantry armaments, command wanted to try and see if they can update their bolt-action rifles rather than have them be obsolete. Uses 30rnd 7.92x57mm magazines. ^reset;
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

A 9 barreled magic volley gun that fires in a burst sequence. Offers a lot more lethality in a short time frame than a standard rifle, but suffers from overheating issue that causes the barrels to degrade rapidly, crippling its accuracy in long range engagements.  ^yellow;Magishot ammunition determines damage and magazine capacity. Fires in accurate 9-burst sequences.^reset;

^#c93d3d;Cannot MISS, but durability heavily impacts accuracy.^reset;
^orange;Volley Gunner: 0.25s PARRY WINDOW | 200HP STABILITY^reset;

A Nariakira rifle with a T30 Bayonet, used as a melee weapon. As the war progressed, bayonet training (and training in general) became shorter, and new recruits were taught just the basics - strike true, strike without fear.
^orange;Has less range than a proper spear, but is faster and more controllable.
^yellow;Parry [ALT-FIRE]: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 40HP STABILITY.^white;
^#FFEEC6;Precise Strike [SHIFT]: Prepare a singular, focused thrust attack that deals high THRUST and BLEED DMG | 10s cooldown.^white;

A dense metal spear for puncturing enemies.
^cyan;Inflicts bleeding^reset;
^cyan;Hunting weapon^reset;

A smart pistol capable of firing exotic projectiles with strong tracking capabilities. Its original prototype appears to date back a millennium, yet due to prolonged technological stagnation within a closed environment (compared to human rates), it is still employed as an operational weapon by Lunar Assault Corps today.
^#EA3C0B;Eternal Empire: Weapon don't require maintenance, and reloading doesn't consume ammunition.^reset;
^green;Double tap Shift to switch to a versatile one-handed grip.^reset;

A strange X'i-formed weapon.
^cyan;Eats Tiles, ^orange;+2 Projectiles^reset;^reset;
^yellow;Poison Rad Gas^reset;

Aggressive variant of Nariakira rifle, featuring rifle grenade implements and a bayonet. Yes, the bayonets were so important for IJA's doctrine that some rifle grenades were developed with attached bayonets in mind.
Uses ^yellow;various 7.7x58mm Stripper Clips.^reset;
^orange;Imperial Sentinel: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY.^reset;
^orange;Delivery Tool: Can fire Koshka T97 Grenades and various IJA Rifle Grenades.^reset;

