The IWI Tavor X95 is an Israeli compact, lightweight bullpup carbine rifle that was created from the need to replace its aging inventory of legacy Galil rifles and to create a new rifle that can be used more effectively in confined spaces by mechanized infantry dismounting from cramped vehicles and in close-quarters combat in tight spaces when compared to larger full sized rifles. Accepts STANAG NATO 5.56x45mm magazines.
^green;Hold "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''This is definitely way better than those ancient designs, trust me!''
For export to the human realm, N.I.C produced a combat shotgun compatible with standard human ammunition. While it also utilized technological methods to enhance weapon performance, but as usual, it was difficult to compete with established human companies in the human realm.
^orange;Magnetic Pellet Alignment: Electromagnets in the chamber greatly reduces shot spread.^reset;
^#EA3C0B;Speed Loader: Reload like mag-feed.^reset;
Accepts 12 Gauge shells

''This is not the war, it's a special military operation.''
Used by the Unitan Special Forces and PMC Group. Based on the Avtomát Spetsiálny Val but without the integral suppressor. Only supports standard AS-VAL 9x39mm Magazines.

 ^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a comfortable two-handed grip.^reset;

''This product does not contain radioactive additives.''
Invented during the early industrial era of humanity, it was reportedly first developed as a stimulant—but was soon discovered to be so refreshing after chilling that it was mass-produced as a common beverage. It gained widespread popularity among humans, though there have always been peculiar individuals who collect its bottle caps— why?
^#7AA8E0;Removes active IGNITION effects.^reset;

''Those corporate enforcers imposed ‘humanitarian’ lockdowns on our colonies under the pretext of controlling the spread of erchius infection''
