C96 pistol was a world-renowned firearm, but it held an even higher status in Warlord-ear China, where it was copied in great numbers and variations, with varying quality of assembly. As befitting of early high-powered semi-automatic pistols, C96 had a wooden holster that could be attached to pistol's handle as a stock. Even the invading Japanese appreciated this pistol, and IJA officers often trophied it.
^yellow;.45ACP conversion of Mauser C96.^reset;
