It is not uncommon for magicians to imbue magic into their weapons. The risks of having uncontrolled magic in a solid object is that it can easily backfire on the user. Most incidents are not fatal as it depends on both the density of magic and type. Wind magic for instance will only cause a light breeze upon backfiring while flame magic has a tendency to burn the user.
