Type 24 ''Chiang Kai-shek'' rifle was a Chinese-made copy of the German Standardmodell rifle, the forerunner of the Karabiner 98k. Full-scale production started in late 1935, but it never managed to fully replace the obsolete Hanyang 88, and Type 24 itself was phased out from frontline service by American weapons like M1 Garand and M1 carbine.
Chambered for ^yellow;7.92x57mm Ammo.^reset;

