^#2080f0;Ceternity - The Heart of Spooks^reset;

The holiday's namesake! Ceternity appears as an abstract, colorful face on posters and decorations throughout alta cities.

No one knows what Ceternity really is - a being? A concept? An aesthetic? But everyone agrees it's the perfect symbol for spooky season!

^#2080f0;Entry by Mina^reset;
^gray;Season 2, Week 12^reset;

Today was absolutely magical! Omnika and I went on the most wonderful date to a nearby ^#2d4c56;koywa resort^reset;~ «

^white;Afternoon:^reset; We walked along the crystal-lined paths, hand-in-hand, watching strizychars dance between ^#497c64;miko koywa^reset; flowers.

^#2080f0;Special Cases^reset;

Some dishes naturally vary during preparation, separate from perfect cooking:

^#20f080;Nia Cocktails^reset; will polarize into Ceternia, Alternia, or Enternia variants. Perfect cooking creates the rare ^#ffa8e8;Staris Cocktail^reset; instead!

^#2080f0;The Moment of Truth^reset;

The transformation happens right after preparation, not while aging. Once a dish starts its aging process, what you have is what you get!

Some dishes are more likely to achieve perfection than others. Complex preparations with multiple components have more variables to align.

^#2080f0;The Octagonal Sign^reset;

The symbol of the cycle - an octagon with one line - represents completion and continuation. Eight sides for eight season halves, one line marking the next step on our shared path forward.

Endings are also beginnings, and every sister matters.

^#20f080;Jack O' Lanterns - Glowing Guardians^reset;

^#20f080;Neonjacks^reset; (carved neonmelons) glow teal-green, while ^#ff8020;Yaajacks^reset; (carved yaara melons) glow orange. Both use natural internal light to create eerie illumination!

These bioluminescent lanterns line streets and doorways, keeping the spooky atmosphere alive all night long.

^#20f080;What is Perfect Cooking?^reset;

When you finish preparing a dish - in that brief window before it begins aging - there's a chance it will develop enhanced properties beyond the base recipe.

Think of it as all the variables aligning perfectly: temperature, timing, ingredient quality, even your mood while cooking!

^#20f080;Words from the Heart^reset;

My dearest sisters,

This past year brought challenges and triumphs. From ^#f02020;EDS^reset; protecting borders, to ^#ffe364;Faradea^reset; exploring frontiers, to every researcher pursuing knowledge - you contributed to our shared story.

^#20f080;Yaara^reset;
Yaara Groves are huge underground megaplants, that spread into large distances and form their own microclimate with different plants and creatures inside.

^#9b2d3f;Warped^reset;
A constantly spreading plant-like matter, that "warps" the surroundings it contaminates. Can often be quite poisonous, and, in some cases, bioluminescent.

^#3ED0E8;Shining Sea^white;

^#3ED0E8;Shining Sea^white; is another marine planet which made up of ^orange;Arcane Water^white;, the main source of ^orange;Magiflux Extract^white;.
In addition to ^#8EEFD6;Arcanium Ore^white;, ^yellow;Atla Gold^white; is also a mineral native to the islands and seabed here.

^#606074;Crew status:^#f02020;

- ^#b81824;You are the only registered security unit of this sector.^#f02020;

- ^#b81824;Acquiring more security units may allow for increased operational efficiency.

^#606478;Shadows - Ghostly Guests^reset;

During Ceternity, altas invite ^#606478;shadows^reset; to join celebrations! These ghostly void creatures fit perfectly into the spooky atmosphere.

Their civilization remains mysterious, but encounters are usually positive - especially when expected! Perfect party guests for spooky season~

^#60c0fc;Arknight^reset;'s arsenal.
Press - change attachments: none, laser, stabilizer (x1.25 dmg);
Hold - launch an Icy Cloud Nade.

^#60c0fc;Warm Scarves^reset;

Special blue scarves are given out by local outposts during Sonaveil! Though some altas prefer to knit their own - these warm cotton clothes have become the symbol of the holiday.

Wearing your scarf shows you're celebrating, and they're perfect for staying cozy during outdoor activities like building snowaltas!

^#60c0fc;When to Celebrate^reset;

Sonaveil happens during cold seasons around the cold solstice on ^#2080f0;alterash prime^reset; planets. The exact timing varies by planet, but it always coincides with the coldest, darkest time of year!

The celebration period usually lasts several weeks around the solstice.

^#6189E3;Turbulent^white;

^#6189E3;Turbulent^white; is a beautiful marine planet. Its seafloor is obiously different from normal ocean planets', as its is full of cracks.
You may notice the ^orange;Pink Aquamarines^white;, the specialties beneath the ground by their pink appearance. They are also one of those elemental minerals.

^#64a5d7;Archetype: Corpo^reset;
Archetype that focuses on high-tech weaponry. By utilizing advanced equipment and technology, you can unleash impressive combat efficiency.^reset;
^#64a5d7;Species: Kappa^reset;
Another subspecies of humanity hailing frome Genskyo, short in stature, and highly enthusiastic about technological research and profit-making.

^#64a5d7;Energetic Riptide [Ability]^reset; - Hold fire to ramp up your ENERGY LEVEL (up to 5). For each level: +7.5% weapon proficiency | lasting 2 seconds | clearing ALL ENERGY LEVEL after reloading.
^#64a5d7;Performance Evaluation [Passive]^reset; - +1 PERFORMANCE POINT for each of the following requirements fulfilled:
[Security] - Kill enemies within 60 blocks - 15s | [Research] - pick up efficiency points dropped by enemies - 15s | [Healthy] - Health above 75% | [Energy] - With 3 or more ENERGY LEVEL | [Advanced] - Using energy or tech weapons | [Repair] - Clearing jams - 30s | [Appearance] - Wearing company (NIC or YFFS) uniforms | [Advertising] - Using company standard (NIC or YFFS) weapons | [Hydrated] - Get wet | 30s | For each level: +5% weapon proficiency | +5Max HP | With 5 or more PERFORMANCE POINT: Gain suppression immunity | +15% weapon proficiency | +1%HP/S | Enemies drop additional credits.
^#64a5d7;Technophile [Passive]^reset; - +15% energy and tech weapon proficiency
^red;Too Young To Die [Penalty]^reset; - Lower max HP (100). When below 10% HP, clear all non-penalty traits for 15s.
^orange;Cucumber Addiction [Penalty]^reset; - All non-penalty traits are inactive if undergoing withdrawal. Must consume cucumber-flavor food to stave off withdrawal.

^#693CF2;Crowned Lacrima^reset;

^yellow;Description^reset;: The crowned lacrima has a very odd appearance. Its main body appears to be a giant eyeball, with a crown of stars floating above. Strange accessories float around the crown, as if it is tied to the creature itself. Any attempts to take the crown have failed.

^yellow;Habitat^reset;: The crowned lacrima lives in two places for most of its life. It lives in the upper atmosphere when hibernating, but re-enters it once it's

^#693CF2;Neostella Moth^reset;

^yellow;Description^reset;: The neostella moth has a dark, nebulous body with bright, accentuating markings and antennae. Its sparkling wings also have unique markings, with spots that look like eyes. The neostella moth uses these brilliant markings in an attempt to scare away predators.

^yellow;Habitat^reset;: The neostella moth is nocturnal and only appears at night. It's favourite habitat is the ^green;Starry Garden^reset;, but it can also be found in the

^#693CF2;Starcrab^reset;

^yellow;Description^reset;: Starcrabs are shiny crabs with large stars stuck in their back. They have bright blue bodies and only six legs due to severe radiation. Although they have four less legs than usual, starcrabs move just fine - in a strange, running-like motion.

^yellow;Habitat^reset;: starcrabs are generally found only in Starry liquid-related environments, such as the ^green;Oasis^reset; or ^green;Ocean^reset; biomes.

^#693CF2;Starite^reset;

^yellow;Description^reset;: The starite is a small floating creature. Its body is shaped like a star, and it glows like one as well. The front of the body has a little face you'd almost think is quite "cute".

^yellow;Habitat^reset;: The starite can live within all forms of the ^green;Starry biome^reset;. With its resilient body, it can withstand most treacherous weathers.

^#693CF2;Stellar Fanfish^reset;

^yellow;Description^reset;: The stellar fanfish is a beautiful creature. Decorated with many wondrous colours, it's is quite the sight! stellar fanfish's fins are wide and long, like a fan. Thus, the name. It appears to have a sort of "innocent smile" on its face.

^yellow;Habitat^reset;: The stellar fanfish prefers to live within ^green;Starry Oases^reset;, but it can also be found floating around in the normal ^green;Starry biome^reset;. It refreshes itself by dipping in starry liquid pools.

