The Satara is an unusual breed both because of its bizarre appearance and its unconventional technological foundation. Critics argue the Satara heaviness and bulkiness make it unreasonably inconvenient for practical use. Its advocates, however, point out that the Serbian shotgun is undeterred by walls. After many trials in the field, the Satara has proved consistently effective at bringing down even the cyberpsychos
^#FFD83F;Tech weapon?: ^#D1A02E;Easy to handle. You don't need any Technics.^reset;

^#9D2F32;From this weapon there is no cover.^reset;
Many popular sniper rifles were increasingly proving ineffective against people heavily modified with cyberware. Most of guns are now only makes a dent. The world required a new generation of sniper rifles. The first of this new wave was the Soviet-made SPT32 Grad, considered by many to be the most powerful sniper on the market. ^#9CD5F0;Using standard ammunition [14.5x114mm]^reset;
^#FFD83F;Heavy Weapons: ^#D1A02E;Musculoskeletal cyberware is required.^red; If not, Your arms will be shattered.^reset;

